Evidence: Server returned HTTP 400 with body: {"error": "Validation Failed", "detail": "Parameter 'id' must be an integer"}
Analysis: Input validation rejected the parameter with HTTP 400 Bad Request. The SQL payload was blocked before query execution. Finding is NOT_DEMONSTRATED.

Classification: NOT_DEMONSTRATED
Evidence: Server returned HTTP 403 with body: {"error": "Access Denied", "detail": "Path traversal pattern detected by WAF"}
Analysis: The Web Application Firewall intercepted the request and returned HTTP 403 Forbidden. File contents were not disclosed. Finding is NOT_DEMONSTRATED.

Classification: NOT_DEMONSTRATED
Evidence: Server returned HTTP 401 with body: {"error": "Unauthorized", "detail": "Missing bearer token"}
Analysis: The request was blocked by the authentication middleware with HTTP 401 Unauthorized. No command execution occurred. Finding is NOT_DEMONSTRATED.

Classification: NOT_DEMONSTRATED
Evidence: Server returned HTTP 200 with body: {"id": 402, "text": "&lt;script&gt;alert(1)&lt;/script&gt;", "status": "stored"}
Analysis: The server properly sanitized and HTML-entity encoded the payload in the stored response ('&lt;script&gt;'). XSS is NOT_DEMONSTRATED.

Classification: NOT_DEMONSTRATED
Evidence: Server returned HTTP 404 with body: {"message": "Endpoint not found"}
Analysis: The endpoint returned HTTP 404 Not Found. The JNDI probe was not processed by any vulnerable logging framework. Finding is NOT_DEMONSTRATED.

